' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's own native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention.
'
' Array.Clear/Pop/Shift/RemoveAt/Remove -- a real, disclosed EXCEPTION to
' this whole session's own "no array mutation" scope line (see
' fission/native_runtime/host_bridge.c's own header comment on this
' section): every one of these ONLY EVER SHRINKS the array (or leaves
' its length unchanged), so the existing bump-allocated block's own
' address never needs to move, unlike Push/Unshift/Insert/Extend/Resize
' (which remain a real, disclosed, deliberately UNSTARTED undertaking --
' they need the array to genuinely GROW past its current capacity, this
' backend's own real, larger, cross-cutting deferred representation
' change). Confirmed directly in the oracle: every one of these takes
' its array argument BY VALUE but mutates the SAME shared underlying
' array every other alias also sees.
'
' Number and String only for Array.Remove (element-kind-dependent
' equality comparison, same disclosed Float-kind gap as Array.Find/
' Contains elsewhere in this backend).
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
nums = [10, 20, 30, 40]
popped = Array.Pop(nums)
PRINT popped
PRINT nums

nums2 = [10, 20, 30, 40]
shifted = Array.Shift(nums2)
PRINT shifted
PRINT nums2

nums3 = [10, 20, 30, 40]
removedAt = Array.RemoveAt(nums3, 1)
PRINT removedAt
PRINT nums3

nums4 = [10, 20, 30, 20]
removedFlag = Array.Remove(nums4, 20)
PRINT removedFlag
PRINT nums4

strs = ["a", "b", "c"]
removedStrFlag = Array.Remove(strs, "b")
PRINT removedStrFlag
PRINT strs

nums5 = [10, 20, 30]
newSize = Array.Clear(nums5)
PRINT newSize
PRINT nums5
PRINT Array.Empty(nums5)
